cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Replication package of Chapters 3 to 6 of the thesis \"Reliability of Machine Learning Outputs in Finance\": Confidex and tavp"
abstract: >-
  The library Confidex, which reconstructs from the probabilities of the members of an ensemble the law
  of a further member and reads it at the operating threshold, and the code that reproduces every number,
  table and figure of Chapter 3 (synthetic ensembles with a known truth) and Chapter 4 (two public fraud
  datasets) of the doctoral thesis "Reliability of Machine Learning Outputs in Finance", together with the
  records, the coding and the analysis script of the systematic review of generative models for financial
  time series in Chapter 5, and tavp, the task-aware validation protocol for generative models of financial
  time series of Chapter 6, with its pre-registration, its known-answer tests and its application to the
  Time-Causal VAE and a Quant GAN.
authors:
  - family-names: Palmacci
    given-names: Luca
    affiliation: "Sapienza University of Rome"
keywords:
  - ensembles
  - per-sample confidence
  - Bayesian inference
  - selective classification
  - fraud detection
  - systematic review
  - generative models
  - financial time series
  - validation
  - pre-registration
version: 0.6.0
license: Apache-2.0
